{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fa489802d9b650f7","name":"OG-9 Homing Spider Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-fa489802d9b650f7","title":"OG-9 Homing Spider Droid","revision":20011,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:01:39Z","sha256":"7204347d31d677d886ac37f01fac4e3474fbbc7089d59dc2114c276f992d710e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20011","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=OG-9%20Homing%20Spider%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fa489802d9b650f7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The OG-Series Droids from the Commerce Guild are employed as mobile heavy weapon platforms prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", and they require only minor modifications for use in the war against ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},". Being essentially a ship reactor on legs, the so-called \"Spider Walker\" is able to mount nearly any weapon for use against opponents.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Homing Spider Droids are often teamed with units of four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dwarf Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dwarf_Spider_Droids"},", which act as spotters for the larger and somewhat less agile OG-9s. The DSD1's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Synchronized Fire Circuits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Synchronized_Fire_Circuits","referenceId":"reference:6a4326b112b7d601"}," relay targeting data to the OG-9, making it more accurate. (In game terms, the Dwarf Spider Droids use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aid Another"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aid_Another","referenceId":"reference:276932074aab1852"}," Action to grant bonuses on the OG -9 attack rolls.)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The OG-9 has a significant weakness in that its legs are not as heavily armored as its main body. Any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Critical Hit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Critical_Hit"}," against an OG-9 that deals damage equal to or greater than its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"}," brings the Spider Droid to an immediate halt and reduces its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," to 0 squares, though it is still capable of attacking. The Spider Droid remains immobile until repaired.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["OG-9 Homing Spider Droid Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walker"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitud